## 6. Background Helpers (`SMAppService`), XPC Security & Distribution

### A. Login Items & Background Agents (`SMAppService`)
- **DO** use `SMAppService.mainApp` for Launch-at-Login and `SMAppService.agent(plistName:)` / `.daemon(plistName:)` for background helpers.
- **DO** check `SMAppService.mainApp.status` (`requiresApproval`, `enabled`, `notRegistered`) and call `SMAppService.openSystemSettingsLoginItems()` when the user needs to approve a background agent in System Settings.

### B. XPC Inter-Process Isolation & Peer Validation
Offload crash-prone parsers, privileged operations, or heavy I/O to an XPC Service (`Contents/XPCServices/`) or helper daemon.
- **DO** enforce cryptographic peer validation using Swift's `XPCListener` / `XPCSession` with `XPCPeerRequirement.isFromSameTeam` (or `NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement(_:)`).
- **DON'T** validate XPC peers using `connection.processIdentifier` (PID)—PIDs are subject to TOCTOU reuse attacks.

### C. Release, Hardened Runtime & Notarization Checklist
- **Sign Inside-Out:** Sign nested binaries (`XPCServices`, `LoginItems`, Sparkle `Installer.xpc`, dylibs, frameworks) with `--options runtime --timestamp` **before** signing the outer `.app` bundle.
- **Notarize & Staple:** Always submit via `xcrun notarytool submit App.dmg --keychain-profile "Profile" --wait` and run `xcrun stapler staple App.dmg` so Gatekeeper succeeds offline.

