## 7. Legacy / iOS-Biased (Banned) -> Native macOS Idiom Lookup

| Legacy / iOS-Biased Pattern (Banned on macOS) | Native macOS Production Idiom |
| :--- | :--- |
| `NavigationStack` as top-level app shell | `NavigationSplitView` (Sidebar + Content + Detail) with `Commands` |
| `TabView` at the bottom of a window | Toolbar-styled `TabView`, segmented picker, or `Settings` scene tabs |
| `.sheet` for non-blocking inspector properties | `.inspector(isPresented:)` or `UtilityWindow` |
| `MenuBarExtra` (`.menu`) with live timers / gauges | `NSStatusItem` + custom `NSPanel` (`.nonactivatingPanel`) |
| `window.close()` inside event handler on reusable overlay | `panel.isReleasedWhenClosed = false` + `panel.orderOut(nil)` |
| Storing raw `URL.path` in `UserDefaults` for user folders | `url.bookmarkData(options: [.withSecurityScope])` + `startAccessingSecurityScopedResource()` |
| `SMLoginItemSetEnabled` or `LSSharedFileList` | `SMAppService.mainApp.register()` / `SMAppService.agent(plistName:)` |
| Checking `NSXPCConnection.processIdentifier` (PID) for auth | `XPCPeerRequirement.isFromSameTeam` or `auditToken` code-signing requirement |
| `xcrun altool` for notarization | `xcrun notarytool submit ... --wait` + `xcrun stapler staple` |
| `NSScreen.main` assumed to be the primary display | `NSScreen.main` is the screen with the *key window*; use `NSScreen.screens.first` for primary display or check `NSEvent.mouseLocation` |
